am converges into a cone within the crystal and is focused to a point on top. The green light is absorbed and spontaneously remitted as red light. Not all of the light is absorbed, and a small portion of the 520 nm laser light transmits through the top, unaltered by the ruby's red color.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARuby_ball_fluorescence_%40_520nm_laser_illumination.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/US_%2420_under_blacklight.jpg/500px-US_%2420_under_blacklight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/US_%2420_under_blacklight.jpg/1280px-US_%2420_under_blacklight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/US_%2420_under_blacklight.jpg/500px-US_%2420_under_blacklight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fluorescent security strip in a US twenty dollar bill under UV light","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUS_%2420_under_blacklight.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Stokes_shift-_Rh6G.png/500px-Stokes_shift-_Rh6G.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Stokes_shift-_Rh6G.png/1280px-Stokes_shift-_Rh6G.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Stokes_shift-_Rh6G.png/500px-Stokes_shift-_Rh6G.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The fluorescent dye, rhodamine 6G, is commonly used in applications such as highlighter pens, dye lasers, and automotive leak detection. The absorption profile is a mirror of the emission profile.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStokes_shift-_Rh6G.png"},{"srcs